<title>USA: Stampeder scraps equity offering.</title>
<headline>Stampeder scraps equity offering.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stampeder Exploration Ltd said early Friday that it has withdrawn its previously announced public offering of common shares.</p>
<p>The Calgary, Alberta-based oil and gas company said it was scrapping those plans because it believes the price offered by the underwriting syndicate does not reflect appropriate value to the present shareholders.</p>
<p>The company said the decisino will require that it revise its capital spending program. Stampeder said it expects to announce a reduced capital expenditure program prior to the end of July.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
